.TH FLATCAM-EVO "1" "October 2026" "FlatCAM Evo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flatcam-evo \- FlatCAM Evo, 2D CAM software for PCB manufacturing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flatcam-evo
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,FILE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
FlatCAM Evo reads the manufacturing files of a printed circuit board (Gerber, Excellon, and the board files of
Altium, KiCad, Eagle, OrCAD/Allegro and Sprint Layout) and makes the G-code for a CNC router, a CNC mill or a laser:
isolation routing, copper clearing, drilling, slot milling, board cutout, solder paste dispensing and more.
It also opens G-code, DXF, SVG, PDF, HPGL2 and images, has editors for Gerber, Excellon and Geometry objects,
and a Tcl shell for scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
Open the file. A project (.FlatPrj) is opened, a script (.FlatScript, .tcl) is run, and Gerber, Excellon and
G-code files are opened by their extension (see the file associations in the Preferences).
.TP
\fB\-\-shellfile\fR=\fISCRIPT\fR
Run the Tcl script file after the program starts.
.TP
\fB\-\-shellvar\fR=\fIVALUE1,VALUE2,...\fR
Define the Tcl variables shellvar_0, shellvar_1, ... with these values, for use in the script.
.TP
\fB\-\-command\fR=\fICOMMANDS\fR
Run Tcl commands separated by semicolons. Quote the commands to protect them from the system shell.
.TP
\fB\-\-headless\fR
Run without a window or an OpenGL canvas. Without \fB\-\-shellfile\fR or \fB\-\-command\fR,
read Tcl commands from standard input.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
In headless mode, 0 indicates success, 1 indicates a failed Tcl command, and 2 indicates an invalid command line.
The Tcl command \fBexit N\fR sets the exit status to N.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBFLATCAM_DATA_PATH\fR
Use this directory for application data instead of the default directory listed below.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.FlatCAM\fR
The preferences, the Tools Database, the recent files lists, the log file and the user preprocessors.
